  "rules": [
    "Same frozen 25 IDs and fixed key for each ranker. Filter results to these IDs before using evaluation.score; keep separate outputs and QA dispositions for all 36.",
    "Annotated retrieval hit requires correct identity or an explicitly allowed exact scene, and inclusive temporal IoU >= 0.5. Predicted IDs require the scorer's predicted-to-annotated bbox association and matching tracks inputs. Never compare raw tracker IDs to annotation IDs.",
    "For static visible attributes/position where the rubric accepts either track or full scene, include the rubric interval and the exact highlighted query frame as well as the explicit exact scene. Report highlighted-target hits and scene alternatives separately; incidental scene visibility does not prove identity retrieval.",
    "Use the numeric approximate bounds as written for temporal-09 (10..30) and temporal-14 (110..120). For temporal-17 any available full scene through cutoff 150 is allowed. For second-05 use the 1..100 span as a retrieval proxy only. Actual QA requires both endpoints.",
    "For second-02 and second-08 the primary key scores the named truck history. Full-evidence coverage must additionally retrieve the stated unhighlighted endpoint scene. Neither component alone establishes a complete bundle. An interval-IoU hit does not certify exact endpoint samples or image content.",
    "Candidate coverage is a ceiling, not model quality. For every actual comparison inventory compute existential match over ALL emitted candidates before scoring/ranking, from the same snapshot and with the same source/identity + inclusive IoU rule. Keep impossible cases in the full denominator; report hit rates conditional on coverage separately.",
    "Keep the gold and this manifest out of all inference, candidate creation, text descriptions, selection and tuning."
  ],
